+# E23 result — pinned-RNG deterministic sampled decode
+
+**Date:** 2026-09-02 · **Branch:** `cm/e23-pinned-sampling` (base: `origin/main` @ `50bad81`,
+spec v0.3b) · **Repo:** `Aefinity-AI/cis2-fp` (private)
+
+## Pre-registered PASS/FAIL (from the lab plan, §2.3)
+
+> PASS = sampled token sequence **and** full probability-chain digest bit-identical
+> x86 vs aarch64, 2 runs each. FAIL = divergence localized to either the PRNG stream
+> or the top-p sort/CDF order — both are spec-fixable findings, not dead ends.
+
+## Verdict: **PASS**
+
+## Commands and outputs
+
+Design memo: `docs/design/CIS2_SAMPLING_DESIGN.md`. Implementation: `src/sampling.rs`
+(`rng_word`, `uniform01`, `sample_pinned`) + `src/main.rs` (`--mode sampled --seed
+<u64> --temperature <f32> --top-p <f32>`).
+
+### Gates (penguin, before any weighted run)
+
+```
+$ cargo test --release
+running 14 tests
+... 14 passed; 0 failed
+running tests/no_mul_add.rs
+test no_mul_add_calls_in_src ... ok
+
+$ ./scripts/no_fma_gate.sh
+PASS: no FMA instructions found in target/release/cis2_ref (0 matches for vfmadd/vfnmadd/vfmsub/vfnmsub/fmadd/fmsub)
+== both FMA gates PASS ==
+```
+
+### Greedy-mode regression check (backward compatibility)
+
+`--mode greedy` (the default) must still reproduce the pinned v0.3b `CIS2_REF`
+digest unchanged — confirms the sampling extension touched nothing on the
+existing path:
+
+```
+$ flock /tmp/aefinity-lab-heavy.lock systemd-run --user --scope -p CPUQuota=60% -p MemoryMax=1800M -- ./target/release/cis2_ref
+prompt_idx=0 runs_identical=true
+CIS2_REF digest=d82743059d1db929e710236fe4ec37f89e6f932524801345a006980f7c3cc9df prompt_idx=0 prompt_toks=4 gen_toks=16 dtype=fp32
+```
+
+Matches `docs/CIS2_SPEC_v0.3.md`'s pinned 16-tok digest exactly.
+
+### Sampled-mode runs on penguin (x86_64), heavy-lane wrapped
+
+Params: `--mode sampled --seed 12345 --temperature 0.8 --top-p 0.95 --gen-toks 16`
+(prompt "Once upon a time", 4 tokens). Two **independent OS process** invocations,
+each also doing its own in-process run1/run2 determinism check (§12.4-style):
+
+```
+$ flock /tmp/aefinity-lab-heavy.lock systemd-run --user --scope -p CPUQuota=60% -p MemoryMax=1800M -- \
+    ./target/release/cis2_ref --mode sampled --seed 12345 --temperature 0.8 --top-p 0.95 --gen-toks 16
+[run1] ... run1_tokens=[6403, 1980, 253, 655, 28, 665, 436, 253, 7436, 1838, 8180, 3365, 20391, 30, 2306, 5732, 288, 835, 725, 1495]
+[run2] ... run2_tokens=[6403, 1980, 253, 655, 28, 665, 436, 253, 7436, 1838, 8180, 3365, 20391, 30, 2306, 5732, 288, 835, 725, 1495]
+prompt_idx=0 runs_identical=true
+CIS2_SAMPLE digest=c8c1d5a69696aff092d46b0a80f0d2575f49191128185fdd0422282578f04d33 mode=sampled seed=12345 temperature=0.8 top_p=0.95 prompt_idx=0 prompt_toks=4 gen_toks=16 dtype=fp32
+
+$ flock /tmp/aefinity-lab-heavy.lock systemd-run --user --scope -p CPUQuota=60% -p MemoryMax=1800M -- \
+    ./target/release/cis2_ref --mode sampled --seed 12345 --temperature 0.8 --top-p 0.95 --gen-toks 16
+prompt_idx=0 runs_identical=true
+CIS2_SAMPLE digest=c8c1d5a69696aff092d46b0a80f0d2575f49191128185fdd0422282578f04d33 mode=sampled seed=12345 temperature=0.8 top_p=0.95 prompt_idx=0 prompt_toks=4 gen_toks=16 dtype=fp32
+```
+
+Two separate process invocations, identical digest: `c8c1d5a69696aff092d46b0a80f0d2575f49191128185fdd0422282578f04d33`.
+
+**Sanity check** (seed sensitivity, not part of the pinned test vector): `--seed 99`
+with the same temperature/top-p produces a *different* token sequence and digest
+(`2f8b7d8553f76f5ad1f6b80349d29ec2c2d45dcc4dfc33b447c33051095aa09d`) — confirms the
+PRNG is actually being consumed, not silently ignored (a bug that would make
+digest-matching trivially/vacuously pass).
+
+### Cross-ISA CI dispatch — `.github/workflows/e23-pinned-sampling.yml`
+
+Pushed on `cm/e23-pinned-sampling`, matrix `ubuntu-latest` (x86_64) ×
+`ubuntu-24.04-arm` (aarch64), target digest pinned from the penguin runs above.
+Run [`33660313802`](https://github.com/Aefinity-AI/cis2-fp/actions/runs/33660313802),
+both jobs green:
+
+```
+x86_64:  CIS2_SAMPLE digest=c8c1d5a69696aff092d46b0a80f0d2575f49191128185fdd0422282578f04d33  runs_identical=true  PASS
+aarch64: CIS2_SAMPLE digest=c8c1d5a69696aff092d46b0a80f0d2575f49191128185fdd0422282578f04d33  runs_identical=true  PASS
+```
+
+Bit-identical: penguin run 1 == penguin run 2 == CI x86_64 == CI aarch64, all four
+`c8c1d5a6...`. No FMA gate and unit-test gate also ran and passed inside the CI job
+before the digest check (same job steps as the sampled-decode step).
+
+## What this proves
+
+CIS-2's "same bits regardless of ISA" claim extends past greedy argmax into a real
+sampling regime (fixed seed, temperature=0.8, top-p=0.95) — the PRNG stream
+(`rng_word`/`uniform01`, pure integer + one correctly-rounded f64 multiply) and the
+top-p sort/CDF walk (explicit-comparator sort, sequential f32 accumulation) both
+reproduce bit-for-bit across x86_64 and aarch64. Per the E18 prior-art sweep, no
+reviewed competitor (RepDL, Thinking Machines `batch_invariant_ops`, SGLang,
+EigenAI) covers temperature/top-p sampling under a pinned-RNG determinism contract
+— they are greedy-only or leave sampling unverified.
+
+## What this does NOT prove / scope notes
+
+- Not folded into `docs/CIS2_SPEC_v0.2.md`/`v0.3.md` as ratified normative text —
+  that is a version-bump (v0.4-candidate) decision, Justin's call per the standing
+  publish/spec-change policy. `docs/design/CIS2_SAMPLING_DESIGN.md` is the memo
+  that would ground that change.
+- Only one (seed, temperature, top_p) tuple is CI-pinned so far. A broader sweep
+  (multiple seeds, temperature/top_p combinations, longer generations up to the
+  32-token upper bound the plan allowed) would strengthen the claim further but
+  was not required to resolve this leg's PASS/FAIL line.
+- No claim about sampled-text *quality* — only about bit-identical reproducibility
+  of whatever tokens the pinned algorithm picks.
+
+## Commits (branch `cm/e23-pinned-sampling`, pushed)
+
+- `4940a1a` design memo
+- `e1de94f` `sample_pinned()` implementation + unit tests
+- `ab476ce` wire `--mode` into `main.rs`, extend receipt format
+- `14e55f8` cross-ISA CI workflow
