@@ -0,0 +1,184 @@
+# CIS-2 sampling design — pinned-RNG deterministic sampled decode (E23)
+
+**Status:** design + reference implementation, non-normative extension of
+CIS-2 v0.2/v0.3b. Does not change `CIS2_REF` (greedy-argmax digest) for any
+existing pinned test vector — this is an additive mode, gated behind
+`--mode sampled`, with its own separate witness digest.
+
+**Relationship to the spec:** CIS-2 v0.2 §0 explicitly lists "Seeded/
+temperature sampling" as a non-goal ("decode is greedy-only (argmax every
+step), matching CIS-1's own non-goal"). This document is the design memo
+that closes that gap — the E20-adjacent competitor-gap finding is that
+every reviewed prior-art system (RepDL, Thinking Machines
+`batch_invariant_ops`, SGLang, EigenAI) is either greedy-only or leaves
+sampling unverified. This is scoped as a v0.4-candidate addendum, not a
+retroactive edit to the ratified v0.2/v0.3b text; §11/§12 of the existing
+spec are unchanged.
+
+## 1. Why counter-based, not sequential-state
+
+A sequential PRNG (e.g. a single `u64` xorshift state advanced once per
+draw) makes step `k`'s output depend on replaying every draw from step 0.
+That is a bad fit for a receipt format whose whole point is that a
+verifier can check step `k` in isolation given the witness chain up to
+that point — and it silently breaks the moment decode needs to skip,
+retry, or re-verify a single step. A **counter-based** generator
+(Philox/Threefry family; here a two-round splitmix64 keyed by
+`(seed, position)`) makes every step's random word a pure function of
+`(seed, position)` alone — reproducible by jumping directly to any step,
+which is the same "no hidden mutable state carried step-to-step" property
+CIS-1/CIS-2 already hold for the forward pass itself (fresh KV-cache reads
+aside, nothing here accumulates PRNG state across steps).
+
+## 2. `rng_word(seed, position)` — the pinned generator
+
+Two rounds of the public-domain splitmix64 mixer (Vigna, 2015; the same
+mixer used by Java's `SplittableRandom` and Rust's `rand_pcg`/xoshiro seed
+initializers). Round 1 folds `position` into `seed`; round 2 re-mixes the
+result, so a one-bit change in either `seed` or `position` fully avalanches
+before any bit is consumed:
+
+```rust
+const GOLDEN: u64 = 0x9E37_79B9_7F4A_7C15;
+
+fn splitmix64_round(x: u64) -> u64 {
+    let mut z = x.wrapping_add(GOLDEN);
+    z = (z ^ (z >> 30)).wrapping_mul(0xBF58_476D_1CE4_E5B9);
+    z = (z ^ (z >> 27)).wrapping_mul(0x94D0_49BB_1331_11EB);
+    z ^ (z >> 31)
+}
+
+pub fn rng_word(seed: u64, position: u64) -> u64 {
+    let mixed_position = splitmix64_round(position);
+    splitmix64_round(seed ^ mixed_position)
+}
+```
+
+All operations are `u64` wrapping add/xor/mul/shift — integer ops are
+exact and identical on every conformant ISA (no float, no FMA question
+applies). `rng_word` is called exactly once per decode step in sampled
+mode; `position` is the same 0-based prompt-relative decode step index
+already used for RoPE (`prompt_ids.len() + step`, cast to `u64`).
+
+## 3. `u64 -> f64` uniform draw
+
+Standard technique: take the top 53 bits (matches an `f64` mantissa
+exactly, so the mapping is exact once computed) and scale:
+
+```rust
+pub fn uniform01(word: u64) -> f64 {
+    ((word >> 11) as f64) * (1.0f64 / (1u64 << 53) as f64)
+}
+```
+
+This lands in `[0, 1)`. `f64` multiply and the `u64 -> f64` cast are both
+IEEE-754-mandatory correctly-rounded operations with no FMA involved (a
+single multiply, not a fused multiply-add) — cross-ISA-safe by the same
+argument §6.1 (`rsqrt_cr`) already makes for correctly-rounded ops. This is
+the only place `f64` appears in the sampling path; everything from the
+softmax logits onward stays `f32` per the existing §3 discipline, and the
+`f32 -> f64` widening used at comparison time (§5 below) is always exact
+(no `f32` value loses precision widening to `f64`).
+
+## 4. `sample_pinned(logits, temperature, top_p, seed, position)`
+
+Pinned steps, in order:
+
+1. **Temperature scale.** `scaled[i] = logits[i] / temperature` — plain
+   `f32` division, sequential index order, no FMA. (`temperature = 0` is
+   rejected by the caller; that degenerates to greedy and should use
+   `--mode greedy` instead.)
+2. **Softmax.** Reuse the existing pinned `softmax_seq` (§6, this crate) —
+   max-subtract, `exp_pinned`, strict left-to-right sequential sum
+   (`sum_seq`), divide. Unmodified from the greedy path's own softmax use
+   in `math.rs`; sampling introduces no new transcendental call.
+3. **Pinned order.** Build `(index, prob)` pairs for all `vocab` entries
+   and sort **by probability descending, ties broken by index ascending**
+   — a fully specified total order regardless of the underlying sort
+   algorithm's stability, via an explicit composite comparator
+   (`b.prob.partial_cmp(&a.prob).then(a.idx.cmp(&b.idx))`), so the same
+   result is produced by any conformant `sort_by` implementation on any
+   ISA. This is the "fixed, documented pairing order" the top-p walk uses
+   — analogous in spirit to how CIS-1 pins block-exponent order.
+4. **Nucleus (top-p) selection.** Walk the pinned order accumulating
+   `cum` by strict sequential `f32` addition (`cum = cum + prob`, same
+   discipline as `sum_seq`) until `cum >= top_p` (inclusive of the
+   crossing element) or the list is exhausted (`top_p >= 1.0` — nucleus is
+   everything). The nucleus is the prefix `[0..=crossing_idx]` in pinned
+   order.
+5. **Renormalize.** `total = ` the exact `cum` reached at the end of step
+   4 (recomputed as a clean sequential sum over just the nucleus, not
+   reused mid-flight, to keep the value auditable independent of early
+   termination bookkeeping). Each nucleus member's final probability is
+   `prob[i] / total` (`f32` division).
+6. **Draw and select.** `u = uniform01(rng_word(seed, position))`. Walk the
+   nucleus in pinned order accumulating `cdf` by sequential `f32` addition
+   of the renormalized probabilities; widen each `cdf` value to `f64`
+   (exact) and select the **first** index where `(cdf as f64) > u`. If
+   floating-point rounding leaves the loop without a crossing (the
+   renormalized `cdf` sum lands a few ULP under `1.0`), select the last
+   nucleus member — the same "never fall off the end" guard a strict `<`
+   argmax scan already needs.
+
+Every operation above is either integer arithmetic (exact, ISA-invariant)
+or a single `f32`/`f64` primitive op (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, comparison) with
+no FMA and no new transcendental — the same conformance argument the rest
+of CIS-2 already relies on. `sample_pinned` calls **zero** new pinned
+polynomials; it is built entirely from operations already proven
+cross-ISA-identical in v0.2/v0.3b (`exp_pinned`, `sum_seq`) plus exact
+integer/comparison arithmetic.
+
+## 5. Receipt extension — `mode=sampled, seed=<u64>`
+
+The existing §12.1 witness chain is unchanged for `--mode greedy` (the
+default — omitting `--mode` reproduces the exact pinned `CIS2_REF` digests
+already in the spec, byte for byte). `--mode sampled` uses a **separate**
+witness stream (not a superset/prefix of the greedy one — this is a
+different decode, not an extension of the same run) that additionally
+binds the sampling parameters **before** the per-step loop, so a verifier
+can detect a receipt claiming the wrong seed/temperature/top-p:
+
+```
+witness.update(b"CIS2_SAMPLE_V1")        # 14-byte domain-separation tag —
+                                          # prevents a sampled-mode witness
+                                          # from ever colliding with a
+                                          # greedy-mode one over the same
+                                          # prompt/weights, even by accident
+witness.update(seed.to_le_bytes())       # 8 bytes, LE u64
+witness.update(temperature.to_bits().to_le_bytes())  # 4 bytes, f32 bit pattern
+witness.update(top_p.to_bits().to_le_bytes())        # 4 bytes, f32 bit pattern
+# ... then weights_sha256 / tokenizer_sha256 / config_sha256 / table_digest /
+#     inv_freq_table_digest / prompt token ids, in the SAME order §12.1
+#     already pins for greedy mode
+# ... then per step: full fp32 logit vector (pre-scale, pre-softmax — the
+#     raw model output, identical construction to §12.1 item 7a) + the
+#     SAMPLED next_token_id, LE u32
+```
+
+Printed as `CIS2_SAMPLE digest=<hex> mode=sampled seed=<u64>
+temperature=<f32> top_p=<f32> prompt_idx=<n> prompt_toks=<n>
+gen_toks=<n> dtype=fp32`, parallel to the existing `CIS2_REF` line.
+
+**What this proves if PASS:** the *sampled* token sequence and the full
+probability-chain digest are bit-identical x86 vs aarch64 for a fixed
+seed — i.e. determinism survives the sampling regime, not just greedy
+argmax. **What a mismatch means:** it localizes to exactly one of two
+places, both independently checkable — (a) the PRNG stream itself
+(`rng_word`/`uniform01`, pure integer + single-op float, should be
+trivially portable) or (b) the top-p sort/CDF walk (§4 steps 3-6, which
+depend on the *forward pass's* logits being bit-identical first — a
+pre-existing, already-proven property from v0.2/v0.3b). Either finding is
+spec-fixable, not a dead end, per the pre-registered plan.
+
+## 6. What this does NOT claim
+
+- Not a new transcendental, not a new spec-normative number for the
+  existing greedy test vector — `CIS2_REF` for `"Once upon a time"` /
+  16 tokens / greedy is unchanged.
+- Not yet folded into `docs/CIS2_SPEC_v0.2.md` §11/§12 as ratified
+  normative text — that requires a version bump (v0.4) and is Justin's
+  call per the standing publish/spec-change policy; this document is the
+  memo that would ground that change, not the change itself.
+- No claim about sampling *quality* (this is not a claim that top-p=0.95
+  sampling produces good text) — only about bit-identical reproducibility
+  of whatever it does produce.
